{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' review-room/output/v2.6_critique/captions.srt\"","aggregated_output":"1\n00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,068\nAn ordinary afternoon at Kneaded A.I.\n\n2\n00:00:05,299 --> 00:00:07,135\nThe team can't agree on the opening line.\n\n3\n00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,400\n“I think the headline should lead with a promise.”\n\n4\n00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:15,900\n“Like — save five hours a week on local marketing?”\n\n5\n00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:17,710\nSomeone presents the fix.\n\n6\n00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:24,410\nThey take it to the founder. Who has notes. A lot of notes.\n\n7\n00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,687\nExcept, there is no team.\n\n8\n00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,179\nEvery role is an agent. One coordinator keeps them in sync.\n\n9\n00:00:36,299 --> 00:00:37,519\nThe debate was a group chat.\n\n10\n00:00:40,299 --> 00:00:41,621\nThe presenter was A.I.\n\n11\n00:00:44,299 --> 00:00:46,581\nEveryone here is an agent. Except the founder.\n\n12\n00:00:48,299 --> 00:00:49,646\nThis is how Kneaded A.I. works.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
