{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"Twist mostly lands now. Act 1 reads convincingly human; the debate shots feel coherent and do not give away “AI team” too early. The founder ending pays off conceptually, but emotionally it is still a little soft: he is present, not yet singular. Isolating him more clearly would make “except the founder” hit harder.\n\nPacing is clear, but the reveal gets slightly over-explanatory. The diagram explains the system, yet its dense labels pull the viewer into parsing instead of feeling the twist. The replay beats are the right idea; they just need sharper visual continuity with the earlier shots.\n\nTop 3 changes:\n1. `t30s/t33s`: simplify the orchestration diagram. Remove or relabel “HUMANS” as “Founder input,” enlarge only three ideas: founder, coordinator, agents.\n2. `t36s`: the group-chat overlay begins as a large dark blank. Have readable messages already visible, matching the exact headline debate from Act 1.\n3. `t42s`: replace the “video-claw” deck with the same Kneaded campaign slide from `t18s`, now clearly auto-generated by an agent.\n\nThe final card works at `t51s`, but its fade starts too dark at `t48s`.\n\n—Codex"}}
